#. 完整操作说明 | 运行
msgid "TXT_0462"
msgstr "[GOALS, NUMBERS, AND COUNTER]\nThe basic goal is to reveal every safe cell; drift groups, pollution nodes, Storm Eyes, and other special mechanics also require their related cells to be resolved. A number counts pollution directly adjacent under the current chapter's rules, and Land pollution nodes count too. The top X/Y means flags used / total cores. Wrong and automatic flags increase X; unflaggable Land nodes are excluded from Y. When every surrounding flag is correct and the count matches, double-click a revealed number in Land, Ocean, or Sky (or press J in Keyboard mode) to expand. In Universe, click a revealed number again.\n\n[MOUSE CONTROLS]\nLand/Ocean: left-click to reveal, right-click to flag, and double-click a revealed number to expand. Sky: left-click to reveal, right-click to flag, drag to rotate, and double-click a revealed number to expand. Universe: left-click to reveal, right-click to flag, and click a revealed number again to expand. In Land, Ocean, and Sky, press C or click the robot when Eco Scan is full, then choose a hidden cell. Cancel with Right Click, Esc, or C; Keyboard mode in Land/Ocean also accepts K. Universe has no Eco Scan. Outside Scan targeting, Esc toggles pause.\n\n[KEYBOARD AND MENUS]\nIn Keyboard mode, Land/Ocean use Arrows or W S A D to move, J to reveal or expand, and K to flag. Sky uses Arrows to select an adjacent face, W S A D to rotate, J to reveal or expand, K to flag, and R to center the selected face. C activates Eco Scan in the first three chapters. Mouse remains available. Universe board play is mouse-only and ignores the Controls setting. Menus use Arrows and Enter/Space. F11 or Alt+Enter changes display mode.\n\n[ECO SCAN]\nIn Land, Ocean, and Sky, each successful reveal/expand action and the first flag placed on each cell add 1 energy. One action still adds only 1 even if it opens several cells, and energy carries between levels. Each level requires one reveal before Scan can be used. The robot's three lights mark 4/8/12 energy. A scanned safe cell is revealed automatically; a Pollution Core is confirmed and flagged automatically. The charge then empties and must refill. Universe has no Eco Scan.\n\n[LEVELS 1–7: LAND, UP TO 8 SQUARE NEIGHBORS]\nLevel 1: 5×5/5 cores; Level 2: 6×6/8; Level 3: 8×8/9 with inoperable ruins ignored by adjacency; Level 4: 9×9/12 with random obstacle clusters.\nPollution nodules on Levels 5–7 cannot be operated and count in nearby numbers. Reveal safe neighbors and correctly flag polluted neighbors to cleanse them. The first action around any uncleansed nodule starts one shared timer for the level. Ordinary actions do not extend it; cleansing one group resets the full time. On timeout, every uncleansed group with progress repollutes its local area plus one outer ring: safe cells close, flags and Scan confirmations clear, and the same number of cores is redistributed inside. Outside reveal states, flags, and core positions stay unchanged; boundary numbers update. Pauses, guides, and interaction locks stop the timer.\nLevel 5: 10×10/13, 1 obstacle cluster, 2 nodules, shared 45 seconds. Level 6: 12×12/17, 2 obstacle clusters, 3 nodules, shared 40 seconds. Level 7: 13×13/20, three roots with 3 nodules each, and the mother tree, shared 60 seconds; cleanse all three roots to cleanse the boss.\n\n[LEVELS 8–14: OCEAN, UP TO 6 HEX NEIGHBORS]\nOnly hexes sharing an edge are adjacent. Coral walls cut number counting, zero expansion, and chording. Level 8: 6×6/7; Level 9: 8×7/10 with 1 wall; Level 10: 9×8/14 with 2 walls.\nLevel 11: 10×9/17 total cores; two drift groups take turns moving every 7 seconds, each with 2 safe buoys and 2 mines. Level 12: 11×10/21 total; three groups move every 6 seconds. Reveal buoys and flag mines. Solving one group stops only that group; an unflagged mine crossing the filter causes failure, and related numbers recalculate after every move.\nLevel 13: 12×11/25 with 1 wall and 2 tidal zones. Level 14: 13×12/30 with 2 walls and 3 zones. Only the lit zone can be played; completion unlocks the next and opens a safe patch. Earlier zones remain playable and boundary numbers recalculate.\n\n[LEVELS 15–21: SKY, SHARED-EDGE SPHERE ADJACENCY]\nPentagons have 5 neighbors and hexagons have 6; only shared sphere edges count, rear faces remain on the same board, and every first reveal is safe. Levels 15–21 use 32/6, 42/8, 92/15, 162/26, 252/40, 362/58, and 492/78 faces/cores.\nOn Levels 17–21, each safe reveal has a one-in-five chance to trigger Breeze Aid, revealing a safe face or auto-flagging a core. Levels 19–21 also have one Cloud Shield: a core hit has a seven-in-ten chance to be blocked and auto-flagged, consuming the shield on success. Levels 20/21 reveal 3/5 Storm Eyes as exploration advances; these Eyes are included in the 58/78 total. Eyes cannot be operated and break automatically when their safe and polluted neighbors are resolved—no double-click required. Break them all to win.\n\n[UNIVERSE EXPEDITION]\nUniverse has no numbered levels, separate map, Eco Scan, or Badge Book, and board play is mouse-only. The left panel shows expedition data; the right panel pauses, starts a new Universe, or returns to Sky. Only glowing links are adjacent; silver lines, cyan curves, and purple wormholes all count.\nEvery first reveal is safe: Boards 1–2 also protect 2 neighbors, Boards 3–4 protect 1, and later boards protect only the chosen node. The ship starts with 2 shields. Hitting pollution first consumes 1 shield and auto-flags it; a hit after shields are gone ends the expedition. Board 7 restores 1 shield, then every 5 boards restores another, up to 2. Revealing every safe star automatically generates the next board.\nEvery genuinely generated board—initial entry, successful advance, or new expedition—adds 1 to the lifetime total. Failure, pause, exit, and UI refresh never reset or duplicate it. The first generation of Board 1,000 freezes the expedition for a one-time perspective crawl and trophy reveal, then opens Badge Hall for placement. Closing the Hall resumes that same board.\n\n[BADGES, BADGE BOOKS, AND BADGE HALL]\nAfter any Land, Ocean, or Sky victory, that level's badge spins and grows at center with a golden glow. Any mouse button, Space, Enter, or a gamepad button stores it in that chapter's Badge Book. From victory, Left Click, Space, Enter, or gamepad continues to the next level/chapter; Right Click or Esc returns to victory; the bottom-right button opens Badge Hall.\nBadge entries on the welcome screen, maps, and Settings all open Badge Hall. The Hall has no Back button: left- or right-click outside the four showcases, or press Esc, to return. Land, Ocean, and Sky covers open their Badge Books; Universe has no button or Badge Book. Before 1,000, asteroids show ones, planets tens, and clusters hundreds. At 1,000, a permanently rotating galaxy and trophy replace those counters while the numeric lifetime total keeps growing.\n\n[NAVIGATION, SETTINGS, AND ASSISTS]\n“Start Journey” opens the Land map and “Badge Hall” opens the Hall. Click a map node once to select and again to enter. From pause, “Back to Level” resumes the current game; normal maps use “Enter Selected Level.” Sky's next chapter enters Universe, and Universe can return to Sky.\nSettings control master volume, BGM, SFX, display mode, mouse/keyboard controls for the first three chapters, and language, and save automatically. Land/Ocean may hit pollution on the first reveal by default. After 2 consecutive first-reveal losses, the next attempt guarantees safety; after 3 consecutive losses within the first 5 moves, the next attempt opens a safe region. Sky and Universe always guarantee the first reveal.\nLand, Ocean, and Sky pause menus can resume, restart, open Level Select, Settings, or this guide, return to the main menu, or quit. Universe pause can resume, start a new Universe, open Settings or this guide, return to the welcome screen, or quit; its right panel separately returns to Sky."

